    "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A2",
    "original_text": "Attributed ASTIS-authored scoped mathematical completion, not a verbatim numbered source theorem.\nE is a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume; rank zero is an explicit extension of the source Euclidean convention. V:E→ℝ is C²; 0<α≤β; α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v; η>0 and βη≤1. μ=volume.tilted(−V), J=Law(X,X+√ηZ) for independent X∼μ and Z∼N(0,I), and ν=J.snd. Finite dimensionality of E does not imply finite dimensionality of L²(ν). There exist a selfadjoint bounded operator T on L²(ν) with the literal ν-a.e. action Tu(y)=∫u(x)S(y,dx), where S(y)=volume.tilted(x↦−V((y+x)/2)−‖y−x‖²/(8η)); a class q=1 ν-a.e. with ⟨q,u⟩=∫u dν for all u; and the actual selfadjoint restriction T₀ to H₀=ker⟨q,·⟩. Set ρ=(1−αη)/(1+αη) and δ=4αη/(1+αη)². The squared defect D₀=I_H₀−T₀² is positive. For every u∈H₀, T₀u=Tu as an ambient class, ‖T₀u‖≤ρ‖u‖, ⟨D₀u,u⟩=‖u‖²−‖T₀u‖² and δ‖u‖²≤⟨D₀u,u⟩. D₀ is a unit in the algebra of bounded continuous linear endomorphisms of H₀; hence it has a bounded inverse on this exact centered space. The original hypotheses force δ>0 and include αη=1. No full-space inverse or positive square root is claimed.\nExact source anchor: PBPS2609.06905v1 AppendixB B1-B5, D1-D2 real L2 stationarity/centering, C4/B15 squared-defect precursor; exact31regions/54items source inventory independently covered.\nSource-route distinction: The selected implementation route proves the squared-defect quadratic identity using selfadjoint contraction. The printed B5 joint P/U block identity has its independent source edges retained; it is not claimed proved by this scalar argument.\nRemaining: SAME actual55 T on L2(nu), selfadjoint/mean preserving/constant fixed, exact complete mean-zero restriction T0, full and centered positive squared defects; real Test uses actual58 rho/delta to prove IsUnit centered squared defect. No Gamma/root/polar/full weakH1/hypocoercivity/dynamics/main/implementation error/cost/composition/fullpaper/Goal admission.",
    "text_sha256": "62cf9acdb59d1bbec7ba366fc3f424264848187edbdc28d208283a26dd1a3ccf"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "Tests.ProximalBPSCenteredDefect.actual_centered_defect_coercive_and_unit",
    "file": "Tests/ProximalBPSCenteredDefect.lean",
    "statement": "\n    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    {V : E → ℝ} {α β : ℝ≥0} {η : ℝ}\n    (hα : 0 < (α : ℝ)) (hαβ : α ≤ β) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)\n    (hH : ∀ x v : E,\n      (α : ℝ)*‖v‖^2 ≤ (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v ∧\n      (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v ≤ (β : ℝ)*‖v‖^2)\n    (hη : 0 < η) (hβη : (β : ℝ)*η ≤ 1) :\n    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n    let J := (μ.prod (stdGaussian E)).map\n      (fun p : E × E => (p.1,p.1+Real.sqrt η • p.2))\n    let ν := J.snd\n    ∃ T : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν,\n      IsSelfAdjoint T ∧\n      (∀ u : Lp ℝ 2 ν, (T u : E → ℝ) =ᵐ[ν]\n        (fun y => ∫ x, u x ∂((volume : Measure E).tilted\n          (fun x => -V ((1/2 : ℝ) • (y+x)) - ‖y-x‖^2/(8*η))))) ∧\n      ∃ q : Lp ℝ 2 ν,\n        (q : E → ℝ) =ᵐ[ν] (fun _ => (1 : ℝ)) ∧\n        (∀ u : Lp ℝ 2 ν, inner ℝ q u = ∫ y, u y ∂ν) ∧\n        ∃ T0 : ((innerSL ℝ q).ker) →L[ℝ] ((innerSL ℝ q).ker),\n          (∀ u : ((innerSL ℝ q).ker), (T0 u : Lp ℝ 2 ν) = T u) ∧\n          IsSelfAdjoint T0 ∧ ((1 : ((innerSL ℝ q).ker) →L[ℝ] ((innerSL ℝ q).ker))-T0*T0).IsPositive ∧\n          (∀ u : ((innerSL ℝ q).ker),\n            ‖T0 u‖ ≤ ((1-(α : ℝ)*η)/(1+(α : ℝ)*η))*‖u‖ ∧\n            inner ℝ (((1 : ((innerSL ℝ q).ker) →L[ℝ] ((innerSL ℝ q).ker))-T0*T0) u) u = ‖u‖^2-‖T0 u‖^2 ∧\n            (4*(α : ℝ)*η/(1+(α : ℝ)*η)^2)*‖u‖^2 ≤\n              inner ℝ (((1 : ((innerSL ℝ q).ker) →L[ℝ] ((innerSL ℝ q).ker))-T0*T0) u) u) ∧\n          IsUnit ((1 : ((innerSL ℝ q).ker) →L[ℝ] ((innerSL ℝ q).ker))-T0*T0)",
    "statement_sha256": "8bc7c56cdbef6468f82261c671ced06b74ba3937e198df55c3926a510b7c375a",
    "compiled": true,
    "formalizer": "root-samplinglib-writer",
    "decoder_context": [
      "The underlying space is a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including zero dimension. The potential is C2 with positive alpha<=beta, both displayed global Hessian bounds, eta>0 and beta*eta<=1.",
      "Measure.tilted is normalized exponential tilting. The displayed joint is the pushforward of the independent product of the tilted law and the standard Gaussian; the marginal is its second-coordinate law. Lp real exponent 2 denotes AE classes of measurable square-integrable real functions. Its dimension need not be finite.",
      "The displayed conditional projection is the L2 conditional expectation onto the second-coordinate sigma algebra. Operator multiplication denotes composition; the typed identity acts on the displayed entire domain. The kernel of innerSL(q) is the full closed real subspace orthogonal to q. An inverse expressed by IsUnit belongs to the algebra of bounded continuous linear endomorphisms of exactly that domain.",
      "The existential operator acts AE by the displayed normalized conditional integral. The constant class, mean pairing and full closed centered restriction are produced conclusions. Both exact displayed constants include the endpoint alpha*eta=1.",
      "IsUnit applies only to the squared defect on the exact centered domain. No full-domain inverse, square-root construction, trajectory, convergence rate for an implemented algorithm, or expected-work statement is present."
