    "statement": "E is a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume; rank zero is an explicit extension of the source Euclidean convention. V:E→ℝ is C²; 0<α≤β; α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v; η>0 and βη≤1. μ=volume.tilted(−V), J=Law(X,X+√ηZ) for independent X∼μ and Z∼N(0,I), and ν=J.snd. Finite dimensionality of E does not imply finite dimensionality of L²(ν). There exist a selfadjoint bounded operator T on L²(ν) with the literal ν-a.e. action Tu(y)=∫u(x)S(y,dx), where S(y)=volume.tilted(x↦−V((y+x)/2)−‖y−x‖²/(8η)); a class q=1 ν-a.e. with ⟨q,u⟩=∫u dν for all u; and the actual selfadjoint restriction T₀ to H₀=ker⟨q,·⟩. Set ρ=(1−αη)/(1+αη) and δ=4αη/(1+αη)². The squared defect D₀=I_H₀−T₀² is positive. For every u∈H₀, T₀u=Tu as an ambient class, ‖T₀u‖≤ρ‖u‖, ⟨D₀u,u⟩=‖u‖²−‖T₀u‖² and δ‖u‖²≤⟨D₀u,u⟩. D₀ is a unit in the algebra of bounded continuous linear endomorphisms of H₀; hence it has a bounded inverse on this exact centered space. The original hypotheses force δ>0 and include αη=1. No full-space inverse or positive square root is claimed.",
